WEBVTT

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.550
Masaru's Erased Memories

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.550
The Lost Bond

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.960
Masaru's Erased Memories!

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.550
The Lost Bond!

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.340
After revealing his plans for Digimon genocide, Kurata defeated Mercurimon.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.590
Masaru and the others tried to oppose Gizmon, a servant of Kurata,

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:25.340
but it was Ikuto's anger that allowed Falcomon to evolve to his Perfect form, Yatagaramon,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.860
and take the Gizmon down.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.140
Transportation complete.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.700
Stop acting all casual and get the hell out already!

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.120
Ikuto.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.020
There's no use crying all the time.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.580
Let's go.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.800
But this is odd.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.410
No one's here.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.510
Damn it, of all the times to be gone...

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.400
What the hell's going on here?

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.660
I received a tip.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.000
It appears that DATS has betrayed us and joined forces with the Digimon.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.240
Kurata set us up.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.910
Daimon Masaru.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.300
Fujieda Yoshino.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.760
Tohma Norstein.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.450
You are dismissed from DATS as of today.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.460
What?

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.340
Please wait!

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.030
Let us talk to the Captain about this first!

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.890
If you're looking for Satsuma-kun, he's already been arrested for national treason.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.590
How incredibly unfortunate.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:45.430
If you had just listened to my orders, this wouldn't have happened.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.480
Kurata!

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.360
You...!

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.100
Get them.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:49.440
Yes, sir!

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.270
Yes, sir!

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.860
Ikuto!

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.520
What are you doing?!

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.000
Let go of me!

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.990
The memory erasing device!

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.450
Master!

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:06.910
Yoshino!

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.780
Aniki!

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.410
Stop!

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.600
Stop it!

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.980
Aniki!!!

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.020
What am I doing here?

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.350
I can't remember...

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.800
Let me out!

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.460
Let me outta here!

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.540
Let me see Ikuto!

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.860
I see.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.650
Just as I thought, Kurata was behind this entire conflict.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:03.740
You knew?

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.700
Satsuma suspected him.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.260
The advancement of his new weapons,

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.340
the mysterious Digimon that defeated SaberLeomon,

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.960
and even the arrangements he made with the Ministry of Confidentiality to re-enter the Digital World...

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.250
All of it went far too smoothly.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.970
Man, what is wrong with humans?!

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:28.370
First they protect Digimon, then they turn around and hurt them. I don't get them at all!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.230
It's Kurata who's the bad guy!

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.140
We in DATS are...!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.390
You be quiet for a bit.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.480
Falcomon.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.770
Let me explain.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.890
The human world and Digital World

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.990
are two individual worlds that formerly did not associate with one another.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:50.660
But recently, the dimensional barrier between them has weakened,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.340
and the Digimon began to wander into the human world.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:59.080
To prevent any unnecessary conflict between the humans and Digimon,

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.830
a special preventative team was formed.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:07.510
That was the Digital Accident Tactics Squad - DATS.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:14.200
Together, with our respective masters, we fought for the peace of both worlds.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.230
We fought with pride as DATS members.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.220
<i>Mega Flame!</i>

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.160
But now that our masters' memories are erased,

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.410
DATS's responsibility has been shattered!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.620
We've lost our purpose to fight.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:52.410
So as you see here in figure A, by working for a living...

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.890
Even the bicycles and automobiles we regularly use...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.500
Wha...!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.980
What is this?

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.640
Yoshino!

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.320
Now on to other news.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.120
I'm coming!

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.900
After two weeks since the government imposed martial law in response to the appearance of the large monsters,

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.740
they have officially announced that it will be rescinded as of today.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:17.300
Their reasons have been founded on an announcement by Professor Kurata, who assured us the return of our safety.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:23.460
After holding a conference with him, the government has expressed much admiration for his strategies.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.580
Professor
Akihiro Kurata

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.590
Professor
Akihiro Kurata

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.830
In our current circumstances...

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.040
Professor
Akihiro Kurata

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.800
Tohma-sama, here is your tea.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.690
Is something the matter?

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.590
No, it's nothing.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.500
Why did you bring two?

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.310
Well...

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.920
That's odd.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.660
I'll be taking this one back.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.570
Why are you all so gloomy?

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:56.310
I don't care at all that Aniki was forced to quit DATS!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.750
Because, he's always needed me for who I am!

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.610
No matter how much we fought,

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.850
or how often we distanced ourselves from each other,

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.460
our bond was never broken!

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.930
<i>I need you too, Aniki.</i>

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.850
<i>Come on! Let's beat this guy!</i>

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.310
<i>Yeah! The both of us!</i>

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.430
<i>Mega Flame!</i>

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.420
<i>Don't lose, GeoGreymon!</i>

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.060
<i>You've got my Digisoul with you!</i>

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:30.150
<i>You did it!</i>

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:36.530
In that case, Yoshino and I have a strong bond, too!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.910
No matter how painful the experience was, we supported each other and overcame it!

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.710
<i>Now, Lilamon!</i>

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.210
<i>Marvel Shot!</i>

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.130
<i>Lilamon!</i>

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.040
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:01.020
My bond with Master is also unbeatable!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.170
<i>Go, Gaomon!</i>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.190
<i>Yes, Master!</i>

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:05.480
<i>There, Gaomon!</i>

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.810
<i>Yes, Master!</i>

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.070
<i>The boxing that Master loves...</i>

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.070
<i>I won't forgive whoever soils that!</i>

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.950
It's the same for me and Ikuto!

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:30.130
Then let's all go and see them!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:30.840
Yeah!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:36.430
Even if their memories are erased, they should be able to remember when they see us!

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.220
Wait.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:42.620
The second we escape from here, we will be labeled as traitors.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.100
Are you sure you still want to go?

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.670
I'm going!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.960
What's most important is protecting something at the risk of your life!

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.570
That's what a man does!

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.650
Of course you'd say that, Agumon.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.270
I guess it's not just your stupidity that resembles him.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.700
What was that?!

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.610
Does everyone else agree?

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.490
Yeah.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.990
Very well.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:17.340
I'm not content to being turned into Kurata's puppet myself.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.340
Great, it's decided!

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.730
First, we need to find a way out of here...

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:22.890
Leave that to me!

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.520
Wait!

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.480
What are you planning...

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.480
To do?!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.520
Baby Burner!

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.700
A fire has broken out in the Digimon experimentation room!

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.130
A fire has broken out in the Digimon experimentation room!

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:42.990
What?

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.750
What's going on?

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.400
Sing a Song!

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.560
Try considering the situation a bit first!

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.280
Oh, who cares! We ended up getting out!

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.920
Anyway, let's get out of here!

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:08.890
You're crazy...

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.760
Agumon and you two, go find Masaru and the others!

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:14.290
Everyone else, follow me!

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.460
The Digimon escaped!

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.950
Block all the exits!

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.240
Everyone...

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:25.660
Falcomon!

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.240
Falcomon!

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:31.670
Ikuto!

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:32.460
Thank goodness!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.360
PawnChessmon!

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.370
Where is Satsuma?

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.050
People from the Ministry of Confidentiality have taken him.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.570
I see.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.380
Shirakawa. Kurosaki.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.510
Take Ikuto and get out of this building.

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:51.310
I will look for Satsuma.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.040
Yes, sir!

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.040
Yes, sir!

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.840
Ikuto-kun, let's go.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.800
No.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.740
I'm getting revenge for Mercurimon.

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:01.630
Let's go, Falcomon!

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:04.840
Ikuto-kun!

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:06.690
Oh, he's such a stubborn blockhead!

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.490
This is bad, Agumon!

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:16.630
We Digimon aren't allowed to be seen by the public!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.590
There's no time for that!

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.590
We have to get back their memories quick!

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.120
Kurata!

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.270
Where are you?

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.770
Stop hiding and come on out!

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:32.890
Kurata!

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.920
No need to shout. I can hear you perfectly.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.160
There you are.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.750
Ikuto, there's something there.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:52.840
Digisoul...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.730
Full Charge!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.980
Falcomon, evolve!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.280
Yatagaramon!

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:30.700
Mikafutsu-no-kami!

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.210
Yatagaramon!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.060
Ikuto-kun!

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.860
Wh-What are they?

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.270
In any case, let's get out of here!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.050
Master!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:37.910
Yoshino.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.650
Thanks for the meal.

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:44.460
Oh, are you already full?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.780
Even with my appetite, this is a little...

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:51.730
Pull yourself together. We're only a three-person family.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:52.930
You're right.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.620
Something must be off with me today.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.890
I'm home!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.790
Aniki!

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:03.640
What the hell?!

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.300
Yay, fried eggs!

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.970
Chow time!

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.010
Delicious!

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:21.040
My head... hurts...

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.580
Hey, frog monster!

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:29.490
What do you think you're doing, barging into people's houses like this?!

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.050
I'm not a frog, Aniki!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.450
It's me, Agumon!

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:35.860
Agu... mon?

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.300
I've heard that name from somewhere...

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.700
Cut the crap!

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.420
I don't remember letting someone like you call me his aniki!

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.910
C'mon, Aniki! Remember!

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:48.440
Stay away from me!

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.760
I have no idea who you are!

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:02.900
Get out!

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.460
Aniki...

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:09.690
I thought you'd remember once you saw me...

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.110
That's it!

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.970
Why'd you bring me all the way over here?

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:22.210
This is a meaningful place where the two of us first met!

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.880
Don't be stupid!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:29.090
This is where you and I fought man-to-man!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.300
Man-to-man?

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:32.890
Yeah!

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:36.160
You stopped my blows without being afraid of me!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.220
You fought me seriously!

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.080
<i>This isn't about win-or-lose!</i>

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.730
<i>This is about fighting man-to-man!</i>

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.040
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.230
<i>It's man-to-man!</i>

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:50.660
<i>I see you're pretty brave.</i>

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:51.360
<i>Come on!</i>

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.150
<i>Right!</i>

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:00.520
I became your follower because I admired that about you!

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.390
Did you really forget about me? Your follower?!

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.880
Master! Please remember!

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.760
The days when we fought together as partners!

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:18.470
We fought together...

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:20.820
Remember, Yoshino!

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:23.480
The days when we lived together!

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.150
We lived together...

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.130
SHUT UP!

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.550
I get so pissed off whenever I see your face!

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:40.790
Just get lost!!

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:49.410
Aniki, you...

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:50.460
IDIOT!

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:10.520
<i>You threw some pretty good punches yourself...</i>

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.120
<i>I'm Agumon.</i>

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.870
<i>Daimon Masaru.</i>

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.490
<i>Nice to meet you, Masaru-aniki!</i>

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:30.790
<i>Aniki?</i>

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:32.260
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.800
<i>You're the first person to acknowledge me as a full-fledged individual, Aniki.</i>

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:40.260
<i>That's why, from now on, I'll be your follower!</i>

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:42.470
<i>No choice then.</i>

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:44.770
<i>I'll go get something, so wait here.</i>

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:47.230
<i>Aniki!</i>

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.520
<i>Listen up!</i>

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.400
<i>Don't move from that spot!</i>

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.640
<i>Okay!</i>

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:53.860
<i>I'll wait right here!</i>

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.860
<i>Agumon...</i>

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.560
<i>You...</i>

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.620
<i>How dare you hurt my follower!</i>

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.520
Aniki! Are you okay?!

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.310
I'm sorry, Aniki! I didn't mean to...

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.020
Agu... mon...

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.150
Aniki...

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:44.970
Aniki!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.740
This is great, you remembered!

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:48.620
Oh, Aniki...

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.050
Stop that, you idiot!

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.080
That hurts!

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:52.010
{Agh! }

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:53.020
Hey!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.600
My, my.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.940
You would have continued living in blissful ignorance if you hadn't remembered.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.440
Gizmon, get rid of them!

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:21.690
Marvel Shot!

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:26.250
Winning Knuckle!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.170
Masaru!

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:35.160
Yoshino!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.240
Tohma!

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:42.050
Impossible!

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.030
I sent Gizmon after them, too!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.560
T-They were defeated...

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.590
You both got back your memories too, right?

